<!--//

   if (document.images) {

      // Load images needed [BACK] button.

      back_on  = new Image(); back_on.src  = "../../buttons/back_on.gif";  
      back_off = new Image(); back_off.src = "../../buttons/back.gif";  
   }

   function TurnOn() {

      // Displays image and updates status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_on.src;
         window.status = 'Go back to previous page';
      }
   }

   function TurnOff() {

      // Displays image and clears status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_off.src;
         window.status = '';
      }
   }

//-->

</SCRIPT>

<H3><CENTER><FONT COLOR="#ffff00"><A HREF="mailto:mwm.poolton@talk21.com">Miles Poolton</A></FONT></CENTER></H3>


Miles has a 1992 K registration 5 door Fiat Tipo 16V. Be brought it for &pound;1500 in
March 2000. It's covered 90,000 miles with a full
service history. The car is completely standard and when Miles drove it he found it
quite flat below 4000 rpm. Miles used to have a lancia Coupe 2000 carb version which
was fantastic. He drove a friends injected version and found it to be flat as well.
Miles has read Guy Crofts Fiat/Lancia twin cam tuning bible and he mentions
that because the injected engines use a plenum chamber they don't have the response
of a one choke per cylinder setup such as twin 45's.
<P>
Miles has fitted TAR-OX 6 groove discs and matching pads.

